.TH ATRIUMD 8 "" "Peios" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
atriumd \- Peios web session host
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B atriumd
.RB [ \-\-unrestricted ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B atriumd
is the single privileged process of Atrium, the browser-delivered interactive
session. It runs as SYSTEM because originating a logon requires it: the
authority's logon socket admits SYSTEM alone. Everything else is deliberately
placed on the far side of that privilege.
.PP
The daemon does three things.
It spawns
.IR /usr/libexec/atrium/atrium-server ,
the network-facing half, under a copy of its own token with every privilege
deleted, joined to it by a single socketpair.
On the server's behalf it holds PGSS Logon conversations with the authority and
keeps the resulting tokens in a session table.
For each successful logon it submits one
.I /usr/libexec/atrium/atrium-session
to peinit as that principal (PSPU \(sc7) and hands the server the socket that
reaches it.
.PP
.B atriumd
never parses HTTP, never impersonates, and never forks as any identity but its
own. Nothing that listens on a port runs as SYSTEM. It reads no registry
configuration of its own; its only configuration is the service definition that
starts it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-unrestricted
Skip the token work, for a development host without KACS. The server and every
session then run as this process's own identity. This is a development switch,
not a deployment mode; the daemon logs a warning saying so on every start.
.SH STARTUP AND SUPERVISION
The installed service definition runs
.B atriumd
at the boot trigger as SYSTEM, requires lpsd, and uses Notify readiness: the
daemon sends
.B READY=1
to the socket named by
.B NOTIFY_SOCKET
once atrium-server has been spawned. Because the listener belongs to the
server, a bind failure appears as the server exiting and
.B atriumd
exiting after it. Its restart policy is Always, which is the recovery path for
everything: sessions do not survive an
.B atriumd
restart, by current decision.
.PP
A logout stops that session's peinit job. peinit closes an idle jobs connection
after 30 seconds (PSPU \(sc7.A), so a connection is opened per operation rather
than held.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NOTIFY_SOCKET
Readiness datagram socket. When unset, no readiness notification is sent.
.TP
.B ATRIUM_JOBS_SOCKET
Overrides the peinit jobs socket, which is
.I /run/services/peinit/jobs.sock
by default. Intended for testing against a disposable jobs endpoint.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/sbin/atriumd
This daemon.
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/atrium/atrium-server
The network-facing half, spawned unprivileged. It owns the listening socket,
which is 0.0.0.0:8080 unless
.B ATRIUM_LISTEN
overrides it.
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/atrium/atrium-session
The per-principal session host, one submitted to peinit per logon.
.TP
.I /usr/share/regim/atriumd-service.reg
Service definition seed. It is inert until an image names it in its registry
autoapply configuration.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Messages are written to standard error, which peinit forwards to the log
collector, and are mirrored to
.I /dev/kmsg
so that
.BR dmesg (1)
and the serial console find them on an image without a collector. A machine
where kmsg cannot be opened still runs.
.PP
Failure to start atrium-server, loss of the control socket, or the server
exiting are all fatal and exit with status 1.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR peinit (8)
.PP
Running this executable on a development host does not constitute a service
test; it requires a configured Peios system with the authority, lpsd and peinit
present.
